[
  {
    "sentence_order": 1,
    "start_time": 7.454,
    "end_time": 12.954,
    "text": "Between 1860 and 1861, 11 southern states withdrew from the United States",
    "translation": null,
    "ipa": null
  },
  {
    "sentence_order": 2,
    "start_time": 12.954,
    "end_time": 16.121,
    "text": "and formed the Confederate States of America.",
    "translation": null,
    "ipa": null
  },
  {
    "sentence_order": 3,
    "start_time": 16.121,
    "end_time": 19.704,
    "text": "They left, or seceded, in response to the growing movement",
    "translation": null,
    "ipa": null
  },
  {
    "sentence_order": 4,
    "start_time": 19.704,
    "end_time": 22.288,
    "text": "for the nationwide abolition of slavery.",
    "translation": null,
    "ipa": null
  },
  {
    "sentence_order": 5,
    "start_time": 22.288,
    "end_time": 23.663,
    "text": "Mississippi said,",
    "translation": null,
    "ipa": null
  },
  {
    "sentence_order": 6,
    "start_time": 23.663,
    "end_time": 27.496,
    "text": "“our position is thoroughly identified with the institution of slavery.”",
    "translation": null,
    "ipa": null
  },
  {
    "sentence_order": 7,
    "start_time": 27.496,
    "end_time": 31.746,
    "text": "South Carolina cited “hostility on the part of the non-slaveholding states",
    "translation": null,
    "ipa": null
  },
  {
    "sentence_order": 8,
    "start_time": 31.746,
    "end_time": 33.662,
    "text": "to the institution of slavery.”",
    "translation": null,
    "ipa": null
  },
  {
    "sentence_order": 9,
    "start_time": 33.662,
    "end_time": 39.079,
    "text": "In March 1861, the Vice President of the Confederacy, Alexander Stevens,",
    "translation": null,
    "ipa": null
  },
  {
    "sentence_order": 10,
    "start_time": 39.079,
    "end_time": 42.079,
    "text": "proclaimed that the cornerstone of the new Confederate government",
    "translation": null,
    "ipa": null
  },
  {
    "sentence_order": 11,
    "start_time": 42.079,
    "end_time": 44.412,
    "text": "was white supremacy, or as he put it,",
    "translation": null,
    "ipa": null
  },
  {
    "sentence_order": 12,
    "start_time": 44.412,
    "end_time": 47.537,
    "text": "“slavery” and “subordination” to white people",
    "translation": null,
    "ipa": null
  },
  {
    "sentence_order": 13,
    "start_time": 47.537,
    "end_time": 50.787,
    "text": "was the “natural and normal condition” of Black people in America",
    "translation": null,
    "ipa": null
  },
  {
    "sentence_order": 14,
    "start_time": 50.787,
    "end_time": 55.037,
    "text": "and the “immediate cause of the late rupture and present revolution.”",
    "translation": null,
    "ipa": null
  },
  {
    "sentence_order": 15,
    "start_time": 55.037,
    "end_time": 57.829,
    "text": "Three weeks after the now-infamous Cornerstone Speech,",
    "translation": null,
    "ipa": null
  },
  {
    "sentence_order": 16,
    "start_time": 57.829,
    "end_time": 59.871,
    "text": "the American Civil War began.",
    "translation": null,
    "ipa": null
  },
  {
    "sentence_order": 17,
    "start_time": 59.871,
    "end_time": 64.663,
    "text": "The conflict lasted four years, had a death toll of about 750,000,",
    "translation": null,
    "ipa": null
  },
  {
    "sentence_order": 18,
    "start_time": 64.663,
    "end_time": 67.038,
    "text": "and ended with the Confederacy’s defeat.",
    "translation": null,
    "ipa": null
  },
  {
    "sentence_order": 19,
    "start_time": 67.954,
    "end_time": 71.496,
    "text": "By 1866, barely a year after the war ended,",
    "translation": null,
    "ipa": null
  },
  {
    "sentence_order": 20,
    "start_time": 71.496,
    "end_time": 75.746,
    "text": "southern sources began claiming the conflict wasn’t actually about slavery.",
    "translation": null,
    "ipa": null
  },
  {
    "sentence_order": 21,
    "start_time": 75.746,
    "end_time": 77.871,
    "text": "Meanwhile, Frederick Douglass,",
    "translation": null,
    "ipa": null
  },
  {
    "sentence_order": 22,
    "start_time": 77.871,
    "end_time": 81.579,
    "text": "a prominent abolitionist and formerly enslaved person, cautioned,",
    "translation": null,
    "ipa": null
  },
  {
    "sentence_order": 23,
    "start_time": 81.579,
    "end_time": 85.038,
    "text": "“the spirit of secession is stronger today than ever.”",
    "translation": null,
    "ipa": null
  },
  {
    "sentence_order": 24,
    "start_time": 85.746,
    "end_time": 87.663,
    "text": "From the words of Confederate leaders,",
    "translation": null,
    "ipa": null
  },
  {
    "sentence_order": 25,
    "start_time": 87.663,
    "end_time": 91.288,
    "text": "the reason for the war could not have been clearer— it was slavery.",
    "translation": null,
    "ipa": null
  },
  {
    "sentence_order": 26,
    "start_time": 91.288,
    "end_time": 94.079,
    "text": "So how did this revisionist history come about?",
    "translation": null,
    "ipa": null
  },
  {
    "sentence_order": 27,
    "start_time": 94.079,
    "end_time": 99.079,
    "text": "The answer lies in the Lost Cause— a cultural myth about the Confederacy.",
    "translation": null,
    "ipa": null
  },
  {
    "sentence_order": 28,
    "start_time": 99.079,
    "end_time": 102.913,
    "text": "The term was coined by Edward Pollard, a pro-Confederate journalist.",
    "translation": null,
    "ipa": null
  },
  {
    "sentence_order": 29,
    "start_time": 102.913,
    "end_time": 106.496,
    "text": "In 1866, he published “The Lost Cause:",
    "translation": null,
    "ipa": null
  },
  {
    "sentence_order": 30,
    "start_time": 106.496,
    "end_time": 109.454,
    "text": "A New Southern History of the War of the Confederates.”",
    "translation": null,
    "ipa": null
  },
  {
    "sentence_order": 31,
    "start_time": 109.454,
    "end_time": 112.538,
    "text": "Pollard pointed out that the U.S. Constitution gave states",
    "translation": null,
    "ipa": null
  },
  {
    "sentence_order": 32,
    "start_time": 112.538,
    "end_time": 116.038,
    "text": "the right to govern themselves independently in all areas",
    "translation": null,
    "ipa": null
  },
  {
    "sentence_order": 33,
    "start_time": 116.038,
    "end_time": 119.496,
    "text": "except those explicitly designated to the national government.",
    "translation": null,
    "ipa": null
  },
  {
    "sentence_order": 34,
    "start_time": 119.496,
    "end_time": 122.913,
    "text": "According to him, the Confederacy wasn’t defending slavery,",
    "translation": null,
    "ipa": null
  },
  {
    "sentence_order": 35,
    "start_time": 122.913,
    "end_time": 127.121,
    "text": "it was defending each state’s right to choose whether or not to allow slavery.",
    "translation": null,
    "ipa": null
  },
  {
    "sentence_order": 36,
    "start_time": 127.121,
    "end_time": 130.413,
    "text": "This explanation effectively turned white southerners’ documented defense",
    "translation": null,
    "ipa": null
  },
  {
    "sentence_order": 37,
    "start_time": 130.413,
    "end_time": 135.746,
    "text": "of slavery and white supremacy into a patriotic defense of the Constitution.",
    "translation": null,
    "ipa": null
  },
  {
    "sentence_order": 38,
    "start_time": 135.746,
    "end_time": 137.871,
    "text": "The Civil War had devastated the country,",
    "translation": null,
    "ipa": null
  },
  {
    "sentence_order": 39,
    "start_time": 137.871,
    "end_time": 140.038,
    "text": "leaving those who had supported the Confederacy",
    "translation": null,
    "ipa": null
  },
  {
    "sentence_order": 40,
    "start_time": 140.038,
    "end_time": 142.538,
    "text": "grasping to justify their actions.",
    "translation": null,
    "ipa": null
  },
  {
    "sentence_order": 41,
    "start_time": 142.538,
    "end_time": 145.829,
    "text": "Many pro-Confederate writers, political leaders, and others",
    "translation": null,
    "ipa": null
  },
  {
    "sentence_order": 42,
    "start_time": 145.829,
    "end_time": 149.413,
    "text": "were quick to adopt and spread the narrative of the Lost Cause.",
    "translation": null,
    "ipa": null
  },
  {
    "sentence_order": 43,
    "start_time": 149.913,
    "end_time": 153.329,
    "text": "One organization, the United Daughters of the Confederacy,",
    "translation": null,
    "ipa": null
  },
  {
    "sentence_order": 44,
    "start_time": 153.329,
    "end_time": 156.454,
    "text": "played a key role in transmitting the ideas of the Lost Cause",
    "translation": null,
    "ipa": null
  },
  {
    "sentence_order": 45,
    "start_time": 156.454,
    "end_time": 158.413,
    "text": "to future generations.",
    "translation": null,
    "ipa": null
  },
  {
    "sentence_order": 46,
    "start_time": 158.413,
    "end_time": 161.538,
    "text": "Founded in Nashville, Tennessee, in 1894,",
    "translation": null,
    "ipa": null
  },
  {
    "sentence_order": 47,
    "start_time": 161.538,
    "end_time": 166.329,
    "text": "the UDC united thousands of middle and upper class white southern women.",
    "translation": null,
    "ipa": null
  },
  {
    "sentence_order": 48,
    "start_time": 166.329,
    "end_time": 171.121,
    "text": "The UDC raised thousands of dollars to build monuments to Confederate soldiers.",
    "translation": null,
    "ipa": null
  },
  {
    "sentence_order": 49,
    "start_time": 171.121,
    "end_time": 173.829,
    "text": "These were often unveiled with large public ceremonies,",
    "translation": null,
    "ipa": null
  },
  {
    "sentence_order": 50,
    "start_time": 173.829,
    "end_time": 177.704,
    "text": "and given prominent placements, especially on courthouse lawns.",
    "translation": null,
    "ipa": null
  },
  {
    "sentence_order": 51,
    "start_time": 177.704,
    "end_time": 181.038,
    "text": "The Daughters also placed Confederate portraits in public schools.",
    "translation": null,
    "ipa": null
  },
  {
    "sentence_order": 52,
    "start_time": 181.038,
    "end_time": 183.913,
    "text": "They monitored textbooks to minimize the horrors of slavery,",
    "translation": null,
    "ipa": null
  },
  {
    "sentence_order": 53,
    "start_time": 183.913,
    "end_time": 186.038,
    "text": "and its significance in the Civil War,",
    "translation": null,
    "ipa": null
  },
  {
    "sentence_order": 54,
    "start_time": 186.038,
    "end_time": 190.954,
    "text": "passing revisionist history and racist ideology down through generations.",
    "translation": null,
    "ipa": null
  },
  {
    "sentence_order": 55,
    "start_time": 191.788,
    "end_time": 195.746,
    "text": "By 1918, the UDC claimed over 100,000 members.",
    "translation": null,
    "ipa": null
  },
  {
    "sentence_order": 56,
    "start_time": 195.746,
    "end_time": 200.204,
    "text": "As their numbers grew, they increased their influence outside the South.",
    "translation": null,
    "ipa": null
  },
  {
    "sentence_order": 57,
    "start_time": 200.204,
    "end_time": 203.121,
    "text": "Presidents William Howard Taft and Woodrow Wilson",
    "translation": null,
    "ipa": null
  },
  {
    "sentence_order": 58,
    "start_time": 203.121,
    "end_time": 206.496,
    "text": "both met with UDC members and enabled them to memorialize",
    "translation": null,
    "ipa": null
  },
  {
    "sentence_order": 59,
    "start_time": 206.496,
    "end_time": 209.579,
    "text": "the Confederacy in Arlington National Cemetery.",
    "translation": null,
    "ipa": null
  },
  {
    "sentence_order": 60,
    "start_time": 209.579,
    "end_time": 212.371,
    "text": "The UDC still exists and defends Confederate symbols",
    "translation": null,
    "ipa": null
  },
  {
    "sentence_order": 61,
    "start_time": 212.371,
    "end_time": 215.746,
    "text": "as part of a noble heritage of sacrifice by their ancestors.",
    "translation": null,
    "ipa": null
  },
  {
    "sentence_order": 62,
    "start_time": 216.246,
    "end_time": 217.913,
    "text": "Despite the wealth of primary sources",
    "translation": null,
    "ipa": null
  },
  {
    "sentence_order": 63,
    "start_time": 217.913,
    "end_time": 220.829,
    "text": "showing that slavery was the root cause of the Civil War,",
    "translation": null,
    "ipa": null
  },
  {
    "sentence_order": 64,
    "start_time": 220.829,
    "end_time": 223.329,
    "text": "the myth about states’ rights persists today.",
    "translation": null,
    "ipa": null
  },
  {
    "sentence_order": 65,
    "start_time": 223.913,
    "end_time": 225.663,
    "text": "In the aftermath of the war,",
    "translation": null,
    "ipa": null
  },
  {
    "sentence_order": 66,
    "start_time": 225.663,
    "end_time": 228.871,
    "text": "Frederick Douglass and his abolitionist contemporaries",
    "translation": null,
    "ipa": null
  },
  {
    "sentence_order": 67,
    "start_time": 228.871,
    "end_time": 232.246,
    "text": "feared this erasure of slavery from the history of the Civil War",
    "translation": null,
    "ipa": null
  },
  {
    "sentence_order": 68,
    "start_time": 232.246,
    "end_time": 234.038,
    "text": "could contribute to the government’s failure",
    "translation": null,
    "ipa": null
  },
  {
    "sentence_order": 69,
    "start_time": 234.038,
    "end_time": 236.329,
    "text": "to protect the rights of Black Americans—",
    "translation": null,
    "ipa": null
  },
  {
    "sentence_order": 70,
    "start_time": 236.329,
    "end_time": 238.788,
    "text": "a fear that has repeatedly been proven valid.",
    "translation": null,
    "ipa": null
  },
  {
    "sentence_order": 71,
    "start_time": 239.204,
    "end_time": 243.454,
    "text": "In an 1871 address at Arlington Cemetery, Douglass said:",
    "translation": null,
    "ipa": null
  },
  {
    "sentence_order": 72,
    "start_time": 243.996,
    "end_time": 246.579,
    "text": "“We are sometimes asked in the name of patriotism",
    "translation": null,
    "ipa": null
  },
  {
    "sentence_order": 73,
    "start_time": 246.579,
    "end_time": 249.163,
    "text": "to forget the merits of this fearful struggle,",
    "translation": null,
    "ipa": null
  },
  {
    "sentence_order": 74,
    "start_time": 249.163,
    "end_time": 253.496,
    "text": "and to remember with equal admiration those who struck at the nation’s life,",
    "translation": null,
    "ipa": null
  },
  {
    "sentence_order": 75,
    "start_time": 253.496,
    "end_time": 255.496,
    "text": "and those who struck to save it—",
    "translation": null,
    "ipa": null
  },
  {
    "sentence_order": 76,
    "start_time": 255.496,
    "end_time": 259.788,
    "text": "those who fought for slavery and those who fought for liberty and justice. [...]",
    "translation": null,
    "ipa": null
  },
  {
    "sentence_order": 77,
    "start_time": 259.788,
    "end_time": 264.121,
    "text": "if this war is to be forgotten, I ask in the name of all things sacred,",
    "translation": null,
    "ipa": null
  },
  {
    "sentence_order": 78,
    "start_time": 264.121,
    "end_time": 265.663,
    "text": "what shall men remember?”",
    "translation": null,
    "ipa": null
  }
]
